# Act of Imagination - LLM lane configuration (the entire model-config surface)
#
# The app talks only to the OpenAI-compatible lane(s) you configure here.
# Nothing in the source names an endpoint or a cloud key: with no lane
# configured, the API routes fail closed (HTTP 501, llm_lane_unconfigured)
# and personal conversation material never leaves your machine.
#
# Lane table:
#   AOI_LLM_<LANE>_<FIELD>
#     LANE  = CHAT | ARRANGE | SYNOPSIS   (one per API route)
#     FIELD = PROVIDER | BASE_URL | MODEL | API_KEY | MAX_TOKENS
#   Shared defaults AOI_LLM_BASE_URL / AOI_LLM_MODEL / AOI_LLM_API_KEY;
#   lane-specific values override per field.
#   PROVIDER v0: "openai" (OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions) only.
#   API_KEY optional - leave unset for local/public endpoints.

# Example: one local model server behind every lane.
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works; a local Ollama server looks like:
#AOI_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#AOI_LLM_MODEL=<served-model-id>
#AOI_LLM_PROVIDER=openai

# Per-lane overrides - point one lane at a different model or server:
#AOI_LLM_CHAT_MODEL=<stronger-chat-model-id>
#AOI_LLM_SYNOPSIS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#AOI_LLM_SYNOPSIS_MODEL=<small-fast-model-id>
#AOI_LLM_ARRANGE_MAX_TOKENS=1024

# Optional cloud persistence (local-first; the app runs without these):
#VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
#VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
